## Why This Is Asked
This asks for a concrete governance approach to align many teams around data contracts, versioning, and regulatory constraints, a frequent real-world pain point in fintech.

## Key Concepts
- Contract driven development
- Data contracts and API versioning
- Cross team governance and automation
- Compliance and incident response

## Code Example
```javascript
// Minimal contract validation skeleton
function validateContract(data, contract) {
  for (const field of contract.requiredFields) {
    if (data[field] === undefined) return false;
  }
  return true;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you measure success and roll out across more teams?
- What are risks and mitigations for contract churn and migration?

## Why This Is Asked
Gauges ability to operationalize privacy across multiple squads and regions while preserving velocity, balancing governance with execution.

## Key Concepts
- Privacy-by-design and DPIA governance
- Data minimization and consent management
- CI gates and artifact templates
- Region-specific privacy budgets and rituals

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo CI gate: enforce privacy checks before merge
function privacyGate(feature) {
  if (!feature.hasDPIA || !feature.consentSchemaValid) {
    throw new Error('Privacy gate failed');
  }
  return true;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you measure fatigue or compliance drift across regions?
- What would you automate to keep DPIA upkeep lightweight for fast-moving features?

